{"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "1. Bone Marrow Harvest and BMDM Differentiation: Euthanize C57BL/6J mice, harvest femurs and tibias, and flush bone marrow into cold DMEM. Perform RBC lysis with ACK lysing buffer for 2\u20135 minutes, filter through a 40 \u03bcm strainer, and seed 25\u201335 \u00d7 10^6 cells per 15 cm dish in complete DMEM (DMEM + 10% FBS + 1% Pen/Strep) supplemented with 20\u201340 ng/mL M-CSF. Culture for 5 days at 37\u00b0C. On day 5, harvest macrophages using cold detachment buffer (2 mM EDTA, 2% FBS in DPBS without Ca/Mg; 20 minutes at 4\u00b0C). Confirm cell purity via flow cytometry for CD11b and F4/80 (ensuring >90% purity). Seed cells into plates at standard densities (e.g., 5.0 \u00d7 10^5 cells/well in 24-well plates or 1 \u00d7 10^6 cells/well in 12-well plates) and rest for 16\u201318 hours in complete DMEM without M-CSF prior to stimulation.\n\n2. Stimulation Conditions:\n- TLR and NOD Agonists: Treat rested BMDMs with LPS (100 ng/mL), LTA (1 \u03bcg/mL), Pam3CSK4 (100 ng/mL), Zymosan (10 \u03bcg/mL), R848 (5 \u03bcg/mL), CpG (500 nM), or MDP (1\u201310 \u03bcg/mL) in complete DMEM.\n- Cytosolic STING Agonists: Formulate ligand-lipid complexes by combining 50 \u03bcL Opti-MEM containing ligand (ISD: 0.5 \u03bcg/well; poly(dG:dC): 0.5 \u03bcg/well; or 2\u20323\u2032-cGAMP: 2.5 \u03bcg/well for 24-well format) with 50 \u03bcL Opti-MEM containing 1.5 \u03bcL lipid transfection reagent. Incubate complexes for 15 minutes at room temperature, add dropwise to wells containing fresh media (final working concentrations: 1 \u03bcg/mL ISD, 1 \u03bcg/mL poly(dG:dC), 5 \u03bcg/mL 2\u20323\u2032-cGAMP), and include mock transfection controls.\n- M2 / Wound Healing: Treat with IL-4 (10\u201320 ng/mL) with or without IL-13 (10\u201320 ng/mL) in complete DMEM without M-CSF.\n- Tolerogenic Efferocytosis: Prepare apoptotic source cells (thymocytes or lymphoid line) via 40 Gy irradiation (6 h incubation) or 1 \u03bcM staurosporine (4\u20136 h incubation). Wash with PBS, verify apoptotic state via Annexin V+/PI- flow cytometry, and co-culture with BMDMs at a 5:1 or 10:1 target-to-macrophage ratio.\n- Tumor Microenvironment Contexts: Treat BMDMs with 20% Tumor Conditioned Media (TCM, processed from tumor tissue homogenates filtered at 0.2 \u03bcm) or 50% Tumor Cell Supernatant (TCS, collected from 80%\u201390% confluent cell cultures).\n\n3. Assay Harvest and Readouts:\n- 8-Hour Readouts: Collect cell culture supernatants in 96-well plates and store at \u221220\u00b0C for cytokine measurement by ELISA. For RNA analysis, wash cells with PBS, lyse in RLT buffer supplemented with \u03b2-mercaptoethanol (20 \u03bcL/mL), store at \u221220\u00b0C, and analyze gene expression by RT-qPCR for targets including Irf5, Irf7, Ifn\u03b11, Arg1, Retnla, Chil3, Mrc1, Il10, Tgfb1, and MerTK.\n- 24-Hour Readouts: Harvest cells and run flow cytometry for activation markers (MHC-I, CD40, CD86) and regulatory/immunosuppressive markers (Arg1, CD206, PD-L1, PD-L2, MerTK, CD36).", "thoughtSignature": ""}], "role": "model"}, "finishReason": "STOP", "index": 0}], "usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 5878, "candidatesTokenCount": 944, "totalTokenCount": 8851, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 5878}], "thoughtsTokenCount": 2029, "serviceTier": "standard"}, "modelVersion": "gemini-3.6-flash", "responseId": "dRn3atWSEfbVjrEP2cqmoQc"}